// One-off (2026-11): adds the "Validation" unit's bank tasks to tasks.json (50 practice, 8 placement).
// Each level has one task for each kind of check, and the last letter of the id says which:
//   i presence, l length, r range, f format, t type (the skills presence, length, range, format, type-check).
// That skill comes first, except on the level 8 tasks that ask again (re-ask first) and the level 10 tasks
// (validation-function first), so their "Show me how" shows the loop or the function.
// Levels 1-2 predict, 3-4 fill in the blanks, 5-6 Parsons, 7-8 write a short check, 9-10 write a full program.
// Python used: input(), .strip(), len(), comparisons, and/or/not, in, .isdigit(), int() after the check, while, and
// def with return True or False (plus indexing and slicing from Strings for format checks). No try/except, regular
// expressions, dictionaries, .isalpha() or .startswith(). Built and checked by tools/unit-tasks.js.
// Run once: node tools/add-validation-unit.js, then build-variants, add-worked-examples, derive-templates and the tests.
